={
  "studyDesignLong": "This study is a retrospective chart review of clinical outcomes in patients with mild to moderate primary open angle glaucoma who have undergone cataract extraction with IOL implantation, OMNI canaloplasty, and Hydrus insertion, or cataract extraction with IOL implantation and OMNI canaloplasty alone, as part of their routine clinical care with a single glaucoma surgeon. The design is intended to evaluate the effect of combining OMNI canaloplasty and Hydrus implantation on glaucoma medication burden compared to OMNI canaloplasty alone, in line with the stated hypothesis and key objectives. Data will be extracted from existing examinations at specified postoperative timepoints, including pre operative and two year postoperative assessments, with outcomes focused on changes in ocular hypotensive medication use, intraocular pressure, visual field parameters, retinal nerve fiber layer thickness, the incidence of secondary surgical interventions, and best corrected distance visual acuity.",
  "methods": "As this is a retrospective chart review, no interventions will be assigned or altered for research purposes, which minimizes treatment related bias. To reduce selection bias, the same predefined inclusion and exclusion criteria will be applied consistently to all eligible patient records. Only adult patients with mild to moderate primary open angle glaucoma who meet the inclusion criteria and do not meet any exclusion criteria will be included in the analysis, and data will be extracted in a uniform manner from existing clinical documentation.",
  "studyProcedure": "Manual and electronic data records will be used to identify eyes that fit the inclusion criteria above. De-identified data from the preoperative examination and any postoperative examinations from up to two yers after surgery will be collected. Data will include: baseline and demographic data, IOP, medication use, and VF data within the 2-year post-operative period.",
